  "signer": "KATHY HOCHUL",
  "text": " \n                APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 102 Chapter 735\n \n      MEMORANDUM filed with Assembly Bill Number 5386-A, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT  to  amend the agriculture and markets law and the soil and\n        water conservation districts law, in  relation  to  establishing\n        the soil health and climate resiliency act\"\n \n    APPROVED\n \n  This  bill will amend the Agriculture and Markets Law to establish the\nSoil Health and Climate Resiliency Act. It will require  the  Department\nof Agriculture and Markets (AGM), in cooperation with the State Soil and\nWater  Conservation  Committee,  to encourage farmers in urban, suburban\nand rural areas to improve soil health, manage  soils  to  mitigate  the\neffects  of  climate change and reduce the overall environmental impacts\nof farms by adopting practices that  conserve  water,  minimize  runoff,\nreduce  greenhouse gas emissions and maximize productivity. To this end,\nAGM will be required by the bill to engage in stakeholder  outreach  and\nestablish  voluntary  standards for soil health reflective of geographic\nregion, soil type and farming methods. The bill also amends the Soil and\nWater Conservation District Law to declare the policy of the Legislature\nto promote the health and resiliency of New York's agriculture soils.\n \n  I agree completely with the policy objectives of the bill, which  will\nprovide  New  York's  agricultural  community  with  additional tools to\nprepare and mitigate the effects of climate change by incorporating soil\nhealth strategies and climate resiliency into  farming  operations.  The\nsoil  health,  climate resiliency and soil research initiatives outlined\nin the bill are the natural next steps that build on  New  York's  solid\nfoundation  through  the  Agricultural  Environmental  Management  (AEM)\nframework and the Climate Resilient Farming Program,  in  helping  farms\nreduce greenhouse gas emissions, increase soil health and better prepare\nfarms for more sustainable operations. The Executive and the Legislature\nhave  agreed  on minor adjustments to the bill to make implementation of\nthe bill more effective.\n \n  On the basis of these changes, I am pleased to sign this bill.\n \n  This bill is approved.                         (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n \n                                ______\n",
  "year": 2021
 },
